# Syntax-aware merges via mergiraf.
#
# Every `merge=mergiraf` attribute below is INERT until the checkout has the
# binary on PATH and `merge.mergiraf.driver` set in its git config. Git says
# nothing when either is missing — it silently falls back to its built-in line
# merge. `.claude/hooks/session-setup.sh` registers the driver for a session
# checkout (via `.github/scripts/install-mergiraf.sh`), and
# `.github/scripts/merge-driver-probe.sh` proves the wiring is live rather than
# merely installed.
#
# Only extensions mergiraf actually parses are listed: an attribute naming a
# language it does not know makes the merge fail over to git's line merge
# anyway, so listing one buys nothing and hides which files are really covered.

# This repo's source and tests.
*.ts merge=mergiraf
*.tsx merge=mergiraf
*.js merge=mergiraf
*.jsx merge=mergiraf
*.mjs merge=mergiraf
*.cjs merge=mergiraf

# Config and CI. `*.json` is also the file type the merge-driver probe merges,
# so removing that line turns the probe red rather than letting it pass inert.
*.json merge=mergiraf
*.yaml merge=mergiraf
*.yml merge=mergiraf
*.toml merge=mergiraf
*.py merge=mergiraf
